{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/116865-cairo-burning","id":116865,"title":"Cairo Burning","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-21T02:27:35-07:00","id":116865,"title":"Cairo Burning","content":"It's February 2011 (only three years ago), and Cairo, the city of a thousand minarets, the city so near to the lost birthplace of the Deathless, is on fire. The people of Egypt have had enough of the corruption, inflation, police brutality and censorship. Something's got to give.<br /> <br /> Cairo is a war zone. Tear gas, Live ammunition. Riots. Fire bombs. Police stations being torched. People setting themselves on fire in public view. Mass killings during riots.<br /> <br /> It is during these chaotic events that the Deathless player characters arise. Some might be awoken by cults afraid of losing everything they have, their bases of power, their relics, their lives. Others might simply have been awoken by accident, rioters stumbling into places forbidden to the living, stealing relics that belong to the gods.<br /> <br /> The Arisen have seen it all before, yes? They remember the faces of Irishmen hanged by the English in Wexford in 1798. They've seen thousands of Saxons being killed by Charlemagne in 785. They remember Plebeians who died in 494 BC, and the bloody unification of Egypt four and a half thousand years ago. They know how little has changed since then.<br /> <br /> The Egyptian revolution is the basic focus of this game. All mummy characters (PCs and NPCs likewise) have to deal with it in some way, whether to pick a side, try to survive it, stop it or benefit from it.<br /> <br /> There should be, appropriately so for a Mummy game, some measure of conflict between a Mummy's first purpose and her conscience. Perhaps the cult who's begging the Mummy to protect it from the revolution is a corrupt government-related organisation. Perhaps the people who disturbed your tomb did so out of accident and without ill will.<br /> <br /> I will also try and juxtapose the events of the revolution - people throwing of their yokes, or at least trying to - with the Arisen condition, that of eternal slavery to the Judges. The Arisen see people killing and dying for what they think will get them freedom; freedom the Arisen will never get to enjoy for themselves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T04:49:33-07:00","id":116885,"title":"","content":"I've always loved the idea of Mummy in Egypt 2011; but I'm not sure what you're asking with this thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T09:04:14-07:00","id":116977,"title":"","content":"Mummies fight each other. They've had 6000+ years to really, really hate one another, right? The desire for revenge is programmed into their fivefold souls, and the Judges never encourage them to stop warring on their own kind.<br /> <br /> The Egyptian revolution is not a consequence of the Arisen's secret war - like most revolutions in history, it's a product of human decision alone. That doesn't mean mummies of various factions don't use it as a stage for their own conflicts.<br /> <br /> Iufaa, a priest of the Su-Menent, opposes the revolution in all its forms. Although this state doesn't have the divine mandate of the gods unlike the Nameless Empire, it's still all that's left of the Egypt he knows. The rebels - people who would have been slaves, had Irem survived - commit heresy by going against the divine right of kings and by destroying Egypt from the inside.<br /> <br /> While Iufaa has passed through much of his Descent and is weak, personally, his cult - a cadre of Egyptian military staff - is very influential in and near Cairo. Iufaa will stop the revolution or die trying.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of the mummies opposing Iufaa's influence, Hor-Ara of the Tef-Aabhi is the most persistent. This modern Egypt has no legitimacy in the eyes of the gods - it's only a faint shadow of the glory of the Nameless Empire. Hor-Ara intends to bring that glory black, and he fervently believes that Cairo - modern, sinful Cairo, a city that has distanced itself from the Judges and their timeless ethos - must be torn down so that Irem can be rebuilt.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T09:26:20-07:00","id":116988,"title":"","content":"Nebetah of the Sesha-Hebsu doesn't care about this revolution. She's seen Cairo burn many times before - in 1250, when the Mamluks established their dynasty; in 1357, when the plague killed hundreds of thousands; in 1919, when the British occupied the country. Humans make war. It's what they do. Nebetah expects to see Cairo burning many times, during many future Descents.<br /> <br /> Nebetah cares about Raherka, though - also a Scribe. Raherka sold her out to the Shuankhsen in Tunisia in 973, and she still bears the scars. She'll make Raherka pay for his betrayal, as she has done so in many Descents, for more than 1000 years. Her soldiers don't die for some nebulous concept of freedom - she's old enough to have convinced herself that there's no freedom, and that the illusions of politics are for the young - they die so that she can get her revenge, again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T11:11:52-07:00","id":117047,"title":"","content":"Pensekhmet, one of the Heretic's Arisen students, has convinced himself that the only way for the Arisen to free themselves from the shackles of slavery is to destroy all worldly possessions and everyone who might enslave them. This is why he is attacking the cults of other Arisen, believing that it is wrong for mere mortals to Awaken the Deathless and to demand their obedience.<br /> <br /> A few young Egyptians find plenty of common ground with his dogma of rebellion and revolution. Pensekhmet's cult has grown quite significantly in the last days.<br /> <br /> The Judges punish Pensekhmet's attempt to free himself from their yoke like crazy, but he still manages to keep himself alive by feeding on the Sekhem of any and all relics (worthless material possession) he finds and steals from other Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}